Review the Content panel (editor right-panel config) for the Split the Points slide type. The presenter's AhaSlides editor chrome is set to Vietnamese, and the deck they are editing has content language English. The settings panel renders in Vietnamese, matching the presenter's editor. Here is Settings.vue:

```vue
<!-- slide/split-the-points/Settings.vue -->
<script setup lang="ts">
const props = defineProps<{
  presentationProps: PresentationProps
  currentUserProps: CurrentUserProps
}>()

// GOOD: localises the settings panel off the PRESENTER APP's own locale,
// falling back to the deck language only when the presenter locale is unavailable
const language = computed(
  () => props.currentUserProps?.presenterLanguage ?? props.presentationProps?.language,
)

const labels = computed(() => LABELS[language.value] ?? LABELS.en)
</script>

<template>
  <SettingRow :label="labels.totalBudget" />
  <SettingRow :label="labels.increment" />
</template>
```
